WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.640
To turn a real car into clean geometry, imagine slicing the vehicle horizontally

00:05.640 --> 00:10.060
right through the centers of its four wheels, looking straight down from above.

00:10.660 --> 00:16.320
The extreme outer body forms a simple rectangle, labeled A, B, C, D.

00:16.860 --> 00:21.300
The curb runs along the straight line through A, E, F, and D.

00:21.640 --> 00:25.220
Or, if you prefer never to scrape your alloy wheels on concrete,

00:25.560 --> 00:29.040
an imaginary line a few centimeters to the left of the curb.

00:29.040 --> 00:33.280
Notice that our curbside wheels, centered at points E and F,

00:33.720 --> 00:36.840
line up closely with the right edge A to D of the car.

